WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:05.859
In A Dance with Dragons, and Season 5 of Game
of Thrones, a knight called Robert Strong

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:10.910
appears in King’s Landing. Qyburn brings
him to Cersei, to join the Kingsguard and

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.620
to fight for her in her upcoming trial-by-combat, where Cersei stands accused of treason. Ser

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.300
Strong has apparently taken a vow of silence,
swearing not to speak “until all of His

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.870
Grace’s enemies are dead and evil has been
driven from the realm”. He doesn’t show

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:30.750
his face, or take off his armour. He apparently
doesn’t eat or drink or “use the privy”.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.670
And he’s huge, “Eight feet tall or maybe
taller”. “[W]here did this man come from?”

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:41.079
[asks] Mace Tyrell. “Why have we never heard
his name before? [Is] he [even really] a knight?”

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:46.030
Who or what is this “silent giant”? To
answer these questions, we need to turn to

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:50.269
Qyburn.
When we first meet Qyburn, he seems nice enough.

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:55.129
He’s described as “fatherly” and grandfatherly, “with warm brown eyes”. But he’s

00:00:55.129 --> 00:01:00.640
actually an incredibly sketchy dude. Qyburn
serves the “Leech Lord” Roose Bolton at

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.470
the notoriously cursed castle of Harrenhal,
and before that, he rides with an infamous

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:11.180
sellsword company, the Brave Companions, also
called the Bloody Mummers. Qyburn himself

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.890
has a reputation for “black magic” and
“necromancy”, having been kicked out

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.470
of the Citadel for “open[ing] the bodies
of the living” “to [better] understand

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:23.040
the nature of death”. The show suggests
he performs “dangerous and unnatural”

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.110
“experiments on living men”. In any case,
he’s a skilled healer, so Qyburn treats

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:32.780
Jaime’s hand – or stump – and comes
with him to King’s Landing. There, he wins

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.890
the trust of Cersei, who confides in him,
tells him her dreams and her secrets at a

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:42.250
time when she feels alone and threatened.
Cersei makes Qyburn master of whisperers, after

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:47.160
Varys disappears with Tyrion.
According to Roose Bolton, Qyburn hopes to

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.380
be made a maester again, and in the show
Kevan calls Qyburn a sycophant. Qyburn has

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.610
cleverly gained the favour of Cersei and a
seat on the small council, but it’s not

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:02.000
like he just wants power. Qyburn tells Jaime,
in the show, that his weakness is “Curiosity”.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.450
He’s a sort of medieval mad scientist,
talking of “proof” and “reason” and

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.579
performing “bold” experiments, out of
a genuine passion for unlocking the secrets

00:02:10.579 --> 00:02:15.140
of the body. In the show he tells Jaime that
the insight from his studies “has saved

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:20.609
many lives”. But, as Cersei says, Qyburn
can do horrors as well as wonders.

00:02:20.609 --> 00:02:27.400
Qyburn shows an interest in the Mountain,
Gregor Clegane, who has been wounded by Oberyn

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.939
Martell’s poisoned spear and is “dying
of the venom … slowly, and in exquisite

00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:36.450
agony”. Cersei wants to put the “mad
dog” down, but Qyburn convinces her to let

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.180
him “tend to” Gregor instead. In the books
he’s very vague about what he plans to do

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.989
with the Mountain, just implies it’s related
to “life and death” and “the black arts”.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:49.930
In the show, Qyburn tells Cersei that he’s
“saving” Gregor, in a “process” that

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:54.549
will “change him somewhat” but not weaken
him. Cersei supports this “work”. She

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:59.700
provides gold, and she also gives Qyburn people,
mostly women, who Cersei wants to get rid

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.409
of – the handmaiden Senelle, some puppeteers, and Falyse Stokeworth – Bronn’s wife’s

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:10.060
sister. We don’t know what Qyburn does with
these women in his dungeon, but we do know

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:16.169
Senelle is “exhausted” , the puppeteers
are “used up” and Falyse is “not entirely

00:03:16.169 --> 00:03:21.260
… comfortable” and “no longer capable
… of feeding herself” before she “die[s]

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:26.139
screaming”. This all seems to be related
to Gregor, who remains with Qyburn “screaming

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:30.499
in the darkness” of the dungeon, or, in
the show, creepily moving beneath a sheet

00:03:30.499 --> 00:03:35.959
in Qyburn’s lab. Before Cersei is arrested
by the High Sparrow, Qyburn promises to “produce”

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:41.219
a “champion” who will “protect [Cersei’s]
son, kill [her] enemies, and keep [her] secrets”,

00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:45.700
someone who “no living man will be able
to withstand”. He also orders a suit of

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:51.109
armour so heavy that the armorer says no man
is strong enough to move and fight in it. After Cersei’s

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:56.950
arrest, Qyburn visits Cersei in her cell,
and in the show, he says “The work continues”.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:03.319
Shortly after, we meet Robert Strong.
So in summary, a “freakish[ly] big” knight

00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:08.499
is dying, a necromancer uses him in creepy
experiments, then produces a freakishly big

00:04:08.499 --> 00:04:13.200
knight who doesn’t seem completely normal
or alive. It’s pretty obvious that Ser

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.759
Robert Strong is Ser Gregor Clegane, somehow
reanimated or kept alive or Frankensteined

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:24.680
together from the parts of Qyburn’s victims,
an eight-foot-tall undead Mountain.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.400
Gregor Clegane has probably dealt more death
and destruction with his own hands than any

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.530
other man in Westeros. Doran Martell says
“If ever a man deserved to die screaming,

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:39.309
it was Gregor Clegane”, and with the rise
of Robert Strong, Gregor might just die twice.

00:04:39.309 --> 00:04:44.690
Some may call that justice, but maybe we
should pity Gregor Clegane. We find out in

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:50.419
Feast that Gregor habitually drinks milk of
the poppy to dull the pain of blinding headaches.

00:04:50.419 --> 00:04:55.740
It may be that Gregor’s extreme brutality
ultimately comes from pain, physical, and

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:01.090
maybe emotional. Like, this man is so fucked
up that he can only find respite from pain

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.860
by inflicting it. So isn’t there something
cruel in prolonging his suffering by raising

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:10.909
him from the dead? In the show, Qyburn is
at Harrenhal when Gregor puts the place to

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:15.889
sword. So maybe Qyburn resents Gregor, and
enjoys having him as his twisted plaything.

00:05:15.889 --> 00:05:20.919
It’s ugly however you look at it, someone
needs to end this silent knight.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:26.580
The question is who? Who will represent the
Faith by fighting Robert Strong in Cersei’s

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.919
trial? To some, the obvious choice is someone
like Lancel Lannister, who would probably

00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:35.930
be obliterated by Ser Strong. But there’s
another theory, that the supposedly dead Gregor

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:42.340
Clegane will fight another supposedly dead
Clegane – Sandor, the Hound. This is called

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.000
Cleganebowl, and is traditionally explained
with dubstep and flashing lights and cries

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.599
of “get hype” but what it basically does
is combine the idea that Robert Strong is

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:56.220
Gregor Clegane with the Gravedigger theory,
that Sandor Clegane is still alive. We won’t

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:00.479
get into Gravedigger here but basically there
is a lot of good evidence that the Hound survives

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:05.840
the wounds that nearly kill him, and becomes
a monk on a secluded island. Cleganebowl claims

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.060
that the Faith in King’s Landing bring the
Hound out of this retirement, and set him

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:15.259
to one last fight – to kill his brother,
the man he’s hated all his life, the man

00:06:15.259 --> 00:06:21.199
who’s been brutally killing and raping across
the realm for years. It may be that, like

00:06:21.199 --> 00:06:26.590
the white walkers’ wights, the undead Gregor
has a weakness to fire. The Hound has a fear

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:32.009
of fire – ever since Gregor gave Sandor
his burns. Maybe the Hound will overcome this

00:06:32.009 --> 00:06:37.580
fear and use fire to kill his abominable brother
in an act of violent redemption. These are

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.330
two of the greatest warriors in Westeros,
returned from the dead to fight for the fate

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:48.759
of Cersei Lannister before all King’s Landing.
Cleganebowl would be pretty fucking sick, and a lot

00:06:48.759 --> 00:06:54.159
of people would love to see it happen. However,
there’s no strong or direct evidence that

00:06:54.159 --> 00:06:58.080
it will happen, and there are a lot of good
reasons to believe it won’t – for starters,

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.710
it wouldn’t really fit the character arc
of Sandor, who has let go of violence and

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:08.039
hatred. He’s embraced a life of peace as
a monk, a crippled monk, who no one even knows

00:07:08.039 --> 00:07:12.650
is still alive, apart from the Elder Brother,
who keeps his identity secret on a remote

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:17.939
island. George R. R. Martin has crafted this
beautiful conclusion to Sandor’s story and

00:07:17.939 --> 00:07:23.550
it just doesn’t fit to have him kill again,
even for a good cause, so Cleganebowl doesn’t

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:29.560
seem likely in the books.
But. HBO does seem willing to sacrifice some

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:34.539
character development if it means they can
fit in a few more flashy fights, as with Jaime.

00:07:34.539 --> 00:07:39.060
And a recent casting announcement suggests
that the next season will feature Septon Meribald,

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.169
the guy who takes Brienne to the Quiet Isle,
where she sees the gravedigger who is probably

00:07:43.169 --> 00:07:48.099
Sandor, which seems weird – would the show
spend screen time on Sandor unless they plan

00:07:48.099 --> 00:07:53.169
to use him for something? HBO is more probably
more aware of and receptive to the Game of

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:57.069
Thrones fandom than George is, who says he
doesn’t read theories and writes his books

00:07:57.069 --> 00:08:02.129
on a computer that isn’t even connected
to the Internet. So maybe, just maybe,

00:08:02.129 --> 00:08:06.590
even if Cleganebowl doesn’t happen in the
books, it could happen in the show, if HBO

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:10.919
knows viewers want it. Perhaps someone needs
to tell them.

00:08:10.919 --> 00:08:16.800
Regardless. The evidence shows that the Mountain
rides again, that Ser Robert Strong is a reanimated

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.120
Gregor Clegane zombie, and whoever he fights
it’ll be really cool to see how this story

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:26.360
plays out in seasons and books to come.
Thanks for watching. As ever, check out the

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:30.639
Song of Ice and Fire subreddit, and Westeros.org,
and all the other great communities where

00:08:30.639 --> 00:08:34.450
Game of Thrones theories originate and are
discussed. You can check out the Gravedigger

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:38.700
video if you’d like to see the evidence
that Sandor Clegane still lives. You can also

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:43.469
subscribe to and follow Alt Shift X for more
explanations and analysis – both on Game

00:08:43.469 --> 00:08:46.339
of Thrones and some other stuff coming soon.
Cheers.

